\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {23.0.1}{\ignorespaces The update that breaks a lazy tag. Top: \(A[1..8]=(3,2,4,5,1,1,5,3)\). Bottom: after \(\mathit  {chmin}(1,8,3)\) the entries \(4,5,5\) clamp to \(3\) (red) and the rest stay. A single tag cannot express ``rewrite only the ones above \(3\)'' -- the change depends on each value -- which is exactly why this family of updates needs the beats bookkeeping of \(\S  \ref {sec:c29-beats}\).}}{1405}{figure.caption.251}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c29-gallery}{{23.0.1}{1405}{The update that breaks a lazy tag. Top: \(A[1..8]=(3,2,4,5,1,1,5,3)\). Bottom: after \(\mathit {chmin}(1,8,3)\) the entries \(4,5,5\) clamp to \(3\) (red) and the rest stay. A single tag cannot express ``rewrite only the ones above \(3\)'' -- the change depends on each value -- which is exactly why this family of updates needs the beats bookkeeping of \(\secref {c29-beats}\)}{figure.caption.251}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {23.0.2}{\ignorespaces The chapter's six-state taxonomy. \emph  {line} and \emph  {path} are the Li Chao engine read statically then on a tree; \emph  {beats} and \emph  {odt} are the two amortised answers to a non-composable clamp; \emph  {map} is the function-composition generalisation of a lazy tag; \emph  {pick} is the boundary that chooses among them and hands off to the neighbouring chapters. Every solved problem sits on one row: CF~631E on \emph  {line}, SPOJ~COT6 on \emph  {path}, CF~896C on \emph  {odt}, CF~750E on \emph  {map}, the Summit CF~932F on \emph  {line}+\emph  {path} merged.}}{1406}{figure.caption.252}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c29-taxonomy}{{23.0.2}{1406}{The chapter's six-state taxonomy. \emph {line} and \emph {path} are the Li Chao engine read statically then on a tree; \emph {beats} and \emph {odt} are the two amortised answers to a non-composable clamp; \emph {map} is the function-composition generalisation of a lazy tag; \emph {pick} is the boundary that chooses among them and hands off to the neighbouring chapters. Every solved problem sits on one row: CF~631E on \emph {line}, SPOJ~COT6 on \emph {path}, CF~896C on \emph {odt}, CF~750E on \emph {map}, the Summit CF~932F on \emph {line}+\emph {path} merged}{figure.caption.252}{}}
