\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {23.1.1}{\ignorespaces One insertion step. The node keeps \(f\), the line that wins at the midpoint \(M\). The new line \(g\) loses at \(M\); since two lines cross at most once, \(g\) can beat \(f\) on \emph  {only one side} of \(M\) -- here the left, where the crossing forces it below. So \(g\) is recursed to that one child and the other half is untouched.}}{1410}{figure.caption.253}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c29-lichao}{{23.1.1}{1410}{One insertion step. The node keeps \(f\), the line that wins at the midpoint \(M\). The new line \(g\) loses at \(M\); since two lines cross at most once, \(g\) can beat \(f\) on \emph {only one side} of \(M\) -- here the left, where the crossing forces it below. So \(g\) is recursed to that one child and the other half is untouched}{figure.caption.253}{}}
